  <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>The controller for personal data processed through this website is Oneward, Inc., a <span class="placeholder">[Delaware]</span> corporation with its registered address at <span class="placeholder">[street address, city, state ZIP]</span>, United States ("Oneward", "we"). You can reach us at <a href="mailto:privacy@getoneward.com">privacy@getoneward.com</a> <span class="placeholder">[confirm mailbox]</span>. <span class="placeholder">[If an EU representative under Art. 27 GDPR or a data protection officer is appointed, add their details here.]</span></p>

  <h2>2. What this policy covers</h2>
  <p>This policy covers personal data we process when you visit getoneward.com or contact us through it. Data we process on behalf of customers during a 30-day analysis or a deployment is governed by the agreements with that customer (NDA and data processing agreement), not by this policy. How we handle that data is described on our <a href="/trust-and-security">Trust & Security</a> page.</p>

  <h2>3. Data we collect and why</h2>
  <h3>When you request a 30-day analysis or contact us</h3>
  <p>If you submit the request form or email us, we process the information you provide: name, work email, and, if you choose to give them, company, location, company website, your current HRIS, and other HR tools you use. We use this to reply to you, to prepare the first call, and to set up the NDA and analysis you asked for. Form submissions are delivered to us through PostHog (see below), where they are linked to your email address.</p>
  <p>Where the GDPR applies, the legal basis is taking steps at your request before entering into a contract (Art. 6(1)(b)) and our legitimate interest in responding to business enquiries (Art. 6(1)(f)).</p>
  <h3>When you visit the site</h3>
  <p>Our hosting provider records technical access data, such as your IP address, browser type, the pages requested, and the time of the request, in server logs for security and to keep the site running. Where the GDPR applies, the legal basis is our legitimate interest in operating a secure website (Art. 6(1)(f)). <span class="placeholder">[Name hosting provider and log retention period.]</span></p>
  <p>We use PostHog to count page views and to receive form submissions. It runs in memory-only mode and sets no cookies, so your visits are not linked across sessions. PostHog receives your IP address, browser type, the pages you view, and the approximate location derived from your IP. Where the GDPR applies, the legal basis is our legitimate interest in understanding how the site is used (Art. 6(1)(f)). There are no advertising or tracking cookies. See the <a href="/cookie-notice">Cookie Notice</a>.</p>

  <h2>4. Who receives your data</h2>
  <p>We share personal data only with service providers that help us run the website and handle enquiries, under contracts that restrict what they may do with it:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Hosting and content delivery <span class="placeholder">[provider, location]</span></li>
    <li>Email and calendar tools used to reply to you and schedule calls <span class="placeholder">[providers]</span></li>
    <li>Analytics and form delivery: PostHog, Inc. (San Francisco, United States), under its data processing agreement. Data is stored in PostHog's US region.</li>
    <li>Scheduling: if you book a demo call, the booking is made through a Google Calendar appointment page (Google LLC) embedded on our site. Google processes the details you enter there under its own privacy policy.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell personal data and do not share it with third parties for their own marketing.</p>

  <h2>5. International transfers</h2>
  <p>Oneward, Inc. is based in the United States. Customer data processed during an analysis or deployment is stored in the EU, in Frankfurt, as described on the <a href="/trust-and-security">Trust & Security</a> page. Enquiry data submitted through this website may be accessed by our team in the United States. Where personal data of people in the EU, EEA, UK, or Switzerland is transferred outside those regions, we rely on the European Commission's standard contractual clauses (and the UK and Swiss equivalents) or on an adequacy decision such as the EU-US Data Privacy Framework where Oneward is certified. <span class="placeholder">[Confirm the transfer mechanism and each provider's location.]</span></p>

  <h2>6. How long we keep data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Enquiry and request data: for as long as needed to handle your enquiry, and then for up to <span class="placeholder">[12 months]</span> unless a contract follows, in which case retention follows that contract.</li>
    <li>Server logs: <span class="placeholder">[retention period]</span>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We keep data longer only where a legal obligation requires it.</p>

  <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
  <h3>Everyone</h3>
  <p>You can ask us what personal data we hold about you, have it corrected or deleted, and object to how we use it, by emailing <a href="mailto:privacy@getoneward.com">privacy@getoneward.com</a>.</p>
  <h3>People in the EU, EEA, UK, and Switzerland</h3>
  <p>Under the GDPR and equivalent laws you have the right to access your personal data, to have it corrected or erased, to restrict or object to its processing, and to receive it in a portable format. Where processing is based on legitimate interest, you may object at any time on grounds relating to your situation. To exercise any of these rights, email <a href="mailto:privacy@getoneward.com">privacy@getoneward.com</a>.</p>
  <p>If you are in the EU, EEA, UK, or Switzerland, you also have the right to lodge a complaint with the data protection authority of your country of residence, workplace, or the place of the alleged infringement.</p>
  <h3>Residents of California and other US states</h3>
  <p>Depending on your state, you may have the right to know what personal information we collect, to request its deletion or correction, and to opt out of its sale or sharing. We do not sell personal information and do not share it for cross-context behavioural advertising. To exercise these rights, email <a href="mailto:privacy@getoneward.com">privacy@getoneward.com</a>. We will not discriminate against you for exercising them.</p>

  <h2>8. Security</h2>
  <p>We protect personal data with technical and organisational measures appropriate to the risk, including encryption in transit, access controls, and least-privilege access for our staff. Our approach to customer data is described on the <a href="/trust-and-security">Trust & Security</a> page.</p>

  <h2>9. Children</h2>
  <p>This website is aimed at businesses and is not intended for anyone under 16. We do not knowingly collect personal data from children.</p>

  <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We will update this policy when our practices or the law change. The date at the top shows the latest version. Material changes will be highlighted on this page.</p>
